  "chapter": 557,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 28 Chapter 557\n \n      MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 5073-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the real property law, in relation to prohibiting\n        mortgagees from requiring mortgagors of certain real property to\n        purchase flood insurance exceeding certain limits\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  legislation  would  prohibit  mortgage  lenders  from  requiring\nprospective  homeowners  to purchase or pay for flood insurance on mort-\ngaged residential real property in an amount that exceeds the  outstand-\ning  principal  balance  of  the  mortgage or that includes coverage for\ncontents. The legislation also requires lenders requiring  flood  insur-\nance  to provide the prospective homeowner with a written notice inform-\ning that the required flood insurance will  only  protect  the  lender's\ninterest in the property.\n \n  I  support  the  goal of this legislation, which would prevent lenders\nfrom burdening prospective homeowners  by  requiring  them  to  purchase\nexcessive  flood insurance as a condition of closing a mortgage. To that\nend, the bill would cap flood insurance coverage at the  amount  of  the\nhomeowner's  economic  interest  in the policy. However, flood insurance\nprovides recovery for physical damage to the property, not the  economic\ninterest of the homeowner. Insurers will pay the amount needed to repair\nor  replace  the  property,  which  is  often lower than the outstanding\namount of the mortgage. Changes are  necessary  to  protect  prospective\nhomeowners by capping the maximum amount of flood insurance that a lend-\ner  may require a prospective homeowner to purchase to the lesser of the\nreplacement value  of  the  residential  real  estate  property  or  the\noutstanding  amount of the mortgage, and to amend the notice required by\nthe legislation.\n \n  I have reached an agreement with the Legislature to enact these chang-\nes.  On the basis of this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2024
 },
